Rhea (Design): Heads-up: noticed weirdness when multiple modals & toasts appear in quick succession on the Console. Top modal closes -> secondary modal opens -> toast from first action appears and briefly covers the new modal footer. Screenshot attached.
Marco (Frontend): Repro: open dataset modal -> submit -> we open confirm modal immediately on success to ask about a follow-up action -> toast slides in bottom-left and sometimes overlaps confirm modal CTAs. Keyboard users can't reach the CTA because the toast is on top layer.
Tess (a11y): Overlap is bad for focus traps. Two issues: 1) Visual overlap blocks hit targets, 2) screen readers sometimes announce the toast then focus is trapped in the new modal so user doesn't get context. For SRs, prefer `aria-hidden` on toasts if they are purely decorative while a modal is active.
Ben (Product): Outcomes we want: maintain density for power users, but never block core CTAs. Also keep toast announcements so users know actions completed. Maybe make toasts avoid modal footprint by default?
Ivy (DevEx): Suggestion: toast placement policy: "avoid-modal" when a modal is open; fallback to bottom-right if avoid area conflicts with safe zones. We can add CSS z-index rules plus a simple geometry check: if toast bounding rect intersects with any visible modal CTA rect, move toast to alternate corner.
Marco (Frontend): Implemented a simple check in the PR branch: computeRects and reposition. Code: 
```
function placeToast(toastEl) {
  const modals = document.querySelectorAll('[data-modal]');
  for (const m of modals) {
    if (rectsOverlap(toastEl.getBoundingClientRect(), m.getBoundingClientRect())) {
      return placeToastAt('bottom-right');
    }
  }
  return placeToastAt('bottom-left');
}
```
Tess (a11y): CSS-only repositioning is fine, but need ARIA semantics: if the toast moves, ensure the `role=status` region is still perceivable. Also, while a modal is open, toasts should default to `aria-hidden=true` and we append the message text to the modal's `aria-describedby` if it relates to the modal action. That avoids SR interruption but preserves context.
Rhea (Design): Visual note: when the toast moves corners it currently flips its pointer/chevron which looks odd; prefer no pointer on toasts, just a floating pill. Also margin tokens: our compact token reduced corner gap from 16px to 6px which makes repositioned toasts cling to modal borders. Can we set a min-gap token 12px?
Ben (Product): Agree on min-gap 12px. Also, when a toast appears near an interactive control, add a subtle focus-visible outline to the control for 400ms to hint it's still actionable. This helps keyboard users notice control availability after visual occlusion.
Marco (Frontend): Implementation plan: 1) geometry check + move to safe corner, 2) use `aria-hidden=true` on toasts when modal has `data-modal-active`, 3) if toast relates to modal action, set modal root `aria-describedby += toastId`, 4) ensure toasts generate unique ids (`toast-<ts>`). Will open PR tonight.
Tess (a11y): One more: avoid using `role=alert` for success toasts (assertive) unless it's critical. Use `role=status` and `aria-live=polite` so SR doesn't interrupt modal flow. For errors use assertive + focus shift to the error.
Ivy (DevEx): I'll add a util in dev-ex library: toast.place({avoidSelectors: ['[data-modal]'], minGap: 12}) and a helper to bind aria-describedby automatically. Adds a small API for product teams.
ci-bot: New PR: frontend#2401 created by marco - "toast: modal-aware placement + aria-describedby"
Rhea (Design): Thanks! Quick follow-up: can we add a small integration test that opens two modals and asserts toasts don't overlap visible CTA bounding boxes? QA can write an e2e.
Marco (Frontend): Yep. I'll wire up a Cypress test. Tagging @Tess for review on the aria bits. ETA for PR review: tomorrow afternoon. :rocket:
